                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy full embeddings
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#special_morphisms Special morphisms
          %p
            Recall from the entry on
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
          %p
            The following definition are the obvious generalizations of the corresponding notions for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          #InnerAnodyneExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The class of morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              generated from the inner horn inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi e
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^e \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
              under
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"}> retract
                  s
            %p
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  inner
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+extensions"} anodyne extensions
          #NormalMonomorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The class of morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              generated from boundary inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]
              under
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
            %p
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dendroidal%20set#NormalMonomorphisms"} normal monomorphisms
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              is an
              %strong inner Kan fibration
              if it has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              with respect to all inner horn inclusions.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda^e[T] &amp;\to&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega[T] &amp;\to&amp; B
                    }
            %p or equivalently with respect to the class of inner anodyne extensions.
          #QuasiOperad.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A dendroidal set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an
              %strong inner Kan complex
              or
              %strong quasi-operad
              if the canonical morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to {*}
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              is an inner Kan fibration.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              of dendroidal sets is an
              %strong acyclic fibration
              if it has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              with respect to all normal monomorphisms.
          #Isofibration.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              of dendroidal sets is called an
              %strong isofibration
              if it
            %ol
              %li
                %p it is an inner Kan fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  the morphism of operads
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d(f) : \tau_d(X) \to \tau_d(Y)
                  is a fibration in the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+operads"} canonical model structure on operads
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  of categories is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
          %h3#the_model_structure The model structure
          #ModelStructureOnDendroidalSets.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              On the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the cofibrations be the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a{:href => "#NormalMonomorphism"} normal monomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects are the weak Kan complexes/
                  %a{:href => "#QuasiOperad"}> quasi-operads
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrations between fibrant objects are precisely the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#Isofibration"} isofibrations
              %li
                %p the weak equivalences form the smallest class of maps that satisfy
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
                  %li
                    %p
                      every
                      %a{:href => "#InnerAnodyneExtension"} inner anodyne extension
                      is a weak equivalence
                  %li
                    %p every acyclic fibration between quasi-operads is a weak equivalence.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#establishing_the_model_structure Establishing the model structure
          %h4#StatementOfTheModelStructure Statement
          #TheModelStructureExistenceAndBasicProperties.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The above choices of cofibrations, fibrations and weak equivalences equips the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              of dendroidal sets with the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                  (with respect to the
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dendroidal%20set#BoardmanVogtTensorProduct"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cisinski Moerdijk, theorem 2.4 and prop. 2.6
            ). We indicate the proof
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ProofOfTheModelStructure"} below
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generating cofibrations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              are the boundary inclusion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I = \{\partial \Omega[T] \hookrightarrow \Omega[T]\}
                    \\,.
            %p A set of generating acyclic cofibrations is guaranteed to exist, but no good explicit characterization is known to date.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> CisMoe, cor. 6.17
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : X \to Y
              between cofibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              is a weak equivalence precisely if for all fibrant objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi τ
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau : dSet(Y,A) \to \tau dSet(X,A)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo :
                    %mi SSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau : SSet \to Cat
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
          %p
            This is in (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk"}> Moerdijk, section 8.4
            ).
          %h4#ProofOfTheModelStructure Proof
          %p
            We state a list of lemmas to establish theorem
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheModelStructureExistenceAndBasicProperties"}
          %p
            The
            %strong strategy
            is the following: we
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+topos"} slice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
            over a normal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            (a model of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+operad"} E-∞ operad
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/E_\infty}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnSlices"}
            below, and the model structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
            itself can then be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphism"} etale geometric morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/E_\infty} \to dSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransferOfTheModelStructure"}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              an inner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+extension"} anodyne extension
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              a normal monomorphism of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes Y \cup B \otimes X \to B\otimes Y
            %p
              (with “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              ” the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 3.1
            ).
          #JFibrations.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J := \{0 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} 1\}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+groupoid"} codiscrete groupoid
              on two objects. We use the same symbol for its image along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo :
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi dSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d i_! : Cat \hookrightarrow dSet
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                \-anodyne extensions
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              are the morphisms generated under
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              from the the inner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+extensions"} anodyne extensions
              and from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout products
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e\} \to J
              with the tree boundary inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{
                    \\partial \Omega[T] \otimes J \; \cup \;
                    \\Omega[T] \otimes \{0\}
                    \\to
                    \\Omega[T] \otimes J
                    \\}_{e \in \{0,1\}, T \in \Omega}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Call a morphism a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                \-fibration
              if it has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against
              = succeed "-anodyne" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, 3.2
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              a
              = succeed "-anodyne" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              a normal monomorphism of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes Y \cup B \otimes X \to B\otimes Y
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "-anodyne" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 3.3
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi dSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{0\} \coprod \{1\} \to J \to \eta
            %p
              defines an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \coprod X \to J \otimes X \to X
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is compatible with slicing, in that for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in sSet
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : X \to B
              a given morphism, we have an interval object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
              given by a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi J
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo ,
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \coprod X &amp;\to&amp; J \otimes X &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{(a,a)}\searrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \swarrow_{a}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              If in the above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is normal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : X \to B
              is
              = succeed "-anodyne," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopies"} left homotopies
              given by the above cylinder defines a notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
            %p
              Say a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to A'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
              is a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                \-equivalence
              if it is a homotopy equivalence with respect to this notion of homotopy, hence if for all
              = succeed "-fibrations" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B
              the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∼
                          %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [A',X]_{\sim_B} \to [A,X]_{\sim B}
            %p is a bijection.
          #ModelStructureOnSlices.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in dSet
              be normal. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
              carries a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              for which
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the weak equivalences are the
                  = succeed "-equivalences;" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %li
                %p the cofibrations are the monomorphisms;
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects are the
                  = succeed "-fibrations" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism between fibrant objects is a fibration precisely if its image in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi dSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
                  is a
                  = succeed "-fibration." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 3.5
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p Notice that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every monomorphism over a normal object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  is normal,
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+topos"} over topos
                  (see there)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ω
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(\Omega)_{/B}
                  may be identified with presheaves on the slice site
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ω
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        PSh(\Omega)_{/B} \simeq PSh(\Omega_{/B})
                        \\,.
            %p
              Therefore for normal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              the slice
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              itself, has a chance to carry a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \otimes (-)
                  is a
                  %em functorial cyclinder
                  in the sense of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure#FunctorialCylinder"} this definition
              %li
                %p
                  the class of
                  = succeed "-anodyne" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure#AnodyneExtensions"} this definition
              %li
                %p
                  so that together these form a
                  %em homotopical structure
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi dSet
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{/B}
                  in the sense of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure#HomotopicalStructure"} this definition
            %p
              The statement then is a special case of
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure#ModelStructureFromHomotopicalStructure"} this theorem
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi dSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty \in dSet
            be any normal dendroidal set such that the terminal morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty \to *
            is an acyclic fibration in that it has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against the tree boundary inclusions.
          %p
            By the general discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+topos"} over topos
            we have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                  %mi dSet
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi dSet
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn ∞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (p_! \dashv p^*)
                  \\,.
                  dSet
                  \\stackrel{\overset{p_!}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{p^*}{\to}}
                  dSet_{/E_\infty}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
            simply forgets the map to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            and where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
            forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          #TransferOfTheModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              of the model structure from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnSlices"}
              exists.
            %p
              This is the model structure characterized in theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheModelStructureExistenceAndBasicProperties"}
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 3.12
            ).
          %p
            So far this establishes the existence of the model structure and that every dendroidal inner Kan complex is fibrant. Below in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#CharacterizationOfTheFibrantObjects"} characterization of the fibrant objects
            we consider the converse statement: that the fibrant objects are precisely the inner Kan complexes.
          %h4#CharacterizationOfTheFibrantObjects Characterization of the fibrations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              A dendroidal set is
              = succeed "-fibrant," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JFibrations"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              between inner Kan complexes is a
              = succeed "-fibration," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibration"} inner Kan fibration
              %li
                %p
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau i^* f
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cisinski Moerdijk, theorem 5.10
            ).
          %h3#MonoidalModelCategoryStructure Monoidal model category structure
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              With respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 3.17
            ).
          #EnrichmentOverItself.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              With respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              corresponding to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
          %h3#Enrichment Other enrichments of the underlying category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (compatibility with the Joyal model structure)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |
              be the tree with a single leaf and no vertex. Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet/\Omega[|]
              is canonically isomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %p
              The model structure on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              induced this way as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+an+overcategory"} model structure on an overcategory
              from the model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              coincides with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          %p
            This is for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk"}> Moerdijk, proposition 8.4.3
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              This model category is naturally an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joyal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              This follows from the fact, cor.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EnrichmentOverItself"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              and the fact that the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Joyal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*: dSet \to sSet_{Joyal}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              However,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is
              %em not
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              %em standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              (but see
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+Cartesian+fibrations"} model structure for dendroidal Cartesian fibrations
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℋℴ𝓂
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{Hom} : dSet^{op} \times dSet \to dSet
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              corresponding to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              normal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an inner Kan dendroidal set, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒽ℴ𝓂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi ℋℴ𝓂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{hom}(A,X) := i^* \mathcal{Hom}(A,X)
            %p
              for the underlying
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒽ℴ𝓂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KanCplx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k(A,X) := Core(\mathcal{hom}(A,X)) \in KanCplx
            %p
              for the maximal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              inside the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
              inside the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi dSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \-^{(-)} : sSet^{op} \times dSet \to dSet
            %p
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{sSet}(K, k(A,X)) \simeq Hom_{dSet}(A, X^{(K)})
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              a fibration between fibrant dendroidal sets (hence an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibration"} inner Kan fibration
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
              on the underlying
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              a normal monomorphism, the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k(B,X) \to k(B,Y) \times_{k(A,Y)} k(A,X)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              between
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 6.7
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is the above is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+extension"} anodyne extension
              (acyclic monomorphism) of simplicial sets, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{(B)} \to Y^{(B)} \times_{Y^{(A)}} X^{(A)}
            %p
              is an acyclic fibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer, cor. 6.9
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              normal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              fibrant, the Kan complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k(A,X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom(A,X)
            %p
              is the correct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              One checks that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \mapsto X^{(\Delta[n])}
              is a fibrant resolution of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{Reedy}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              and
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
              the latter is therefore given by the simplicial set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    n \mapsto Hom_{dSet}(A, X^{(\Delta[n])})
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "-definition" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{(\Delta[n])}
              this is isomorphic to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots = Hom_{sSet}(\Delta[n], k(A,X)) = k(A,X)_n
                    \\,.
          %h3#relation_to_other_model_structures Relation to other model structures
          %p We discuss the relation of the model structure on dendroidal sets to other model category structures for operads.
          %p
            See the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+-+models+for+%28infinity%2C1%29-operads"} table - models for (infinity,1)-operads
            for an overview.
          %h4#model_structure_for_quasicategories Model structure for quasi-categories
          .num_proposition
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi dSet
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi j
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi j
                            %mo !
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (j_! \dashv j^*) :
                    dSet
                    \\stackrel{\overset{j_!}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{j^*}{\to}}
                    sSet
            %p
              induced from the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Delta \hookrightarrow \Omega
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between the above model structure on dendroidal sets, and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              By the proof of (
              %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, cor. 2.10
              ) the model structure for quasi-categories is in fact the restriction, along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_!
              is left Quillen.
          %h4#RelationToModelStructureForDendroidalCompleteSegal Model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            (see there). A crucial step in the proof is the following expression of the acyclic cofibrations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi dSet
                    %mi CM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
            in terms of the dendroidal interval
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_d
            as follows.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p The class of acyclic cofibrations between normal dendroidal sets is the smallest class of morphisms between normal dendroidal sets
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  which contains the
                  = succeed "-anodyne" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %li
                %p
                  with left cancellation property: if a composite
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi i
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{i}{\to} \stackrel{j}{\to}
                  is in the class and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  is, then so is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cis-Moer 09, prop. 3.16
            )
          %h4#RelationToModelStrictureOnSimplicialOperads Model structure on simplicial operads
          %p
            There exists also a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+operads"} model structure on simplicial operads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the model structure on dendroidal sets.
          %p
            This Quillen equivalence is an operadic generalization of the Quillen equivalence between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              There exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi hcN
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Operad
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi hcN
                            %mi d
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mo !
                    %mi dSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (W_! \dashv hcN_d)
                    \:
                    sSet Operad
                    \\stackrel{\overset{W_!}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{hcN_d}{\to}}
                    dSet
                    \\,,
            %p
              Whise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+homotopy+coherent+nerve"} dendroidal homotopy coherent nerve
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the model structure on dendroidal sets, and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+operads"} model structure on simplicial operads
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk11"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk 11, theorem 815
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Under the inclusions (see the discussion at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi sSet
                            %mi Cat
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi sSet
                            %mi Operad
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi hcN
                                    %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi W
                                    %mo !
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi sSet
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi dSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    sSet Cat &amp;\hookrightarrow &amp; sSet Operad
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{hcN_d}}\downarrow \uparrow^{\mathrlap{W_!}}
                    \\\
                    sSet \simeq dSet/\eta &amp;\hookrightarrow &amp; dSet
                    }
            %p
              this restricts to the Quillen equivalence between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-categories"} model structure on sSet-categories
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
              discussed at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+quasi-categories+and+simplicial+categories"} relation between quasi-categories and simplicial categories
          %h4#model_structure_on_operads
            Model structure on
            = succeed "-Operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Write
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Operad"} Operad
              for the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operads"} symmetric operads
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal nerve adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Operad
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mi d
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mi d
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\tau_d \dashv N_d) :
                    Operad
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\tau_d}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{N_d}{\to}}
                    dSet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between the model structure on dendroidal sets, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnDendroidalSets"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+Operad"} canonical model structure on Operad
            %p
              Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_d
              detects and preserves weak equivalences, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_d
              preserves weak equivalences.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk09"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk 09, prop. 2.5
            ).
          %h4#model_structure_for_symmetric_monoidal_categories
            Model structure for symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_15 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi id
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi id
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi He
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dSet_{CM}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{id}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{id}{\to}}
                    dSet_{He}
            %p
              which exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+left+fibrations"} model structure for dendroidal left fibrations
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              of the Cisinski-Moerdijk model structure on dendroidal sets.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Heuts"}> Heuts, remark 6.8.0.2
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+Operad"}> canonical model structure on Operad
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+-+models+for+%28infinity%2C1%29-operads"} table - models for (infinity,1)-operads
          %h2#references References
          %p A useful discussion of of the model structure on dendroidal sets is section 8 of
          %ul#Moerdijk
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              %em Lectures on dendroidal sets
              , lectures given at the Barcelona workshop on
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/HigherCategories/"} Simplicial methods in higher categories
              (2008) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.crm.es/Publications/quaderns/Quadern45-1.pdf"}> preliminary writeup
              )
          %p An expanded and polished version has meanwhile been written up by Javier Guitiérrez and should appear in print soon. An electronic copy is probably available on request.
          %p The model structure was originally given in
          %ul#CisinskiMoerdijk09
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Dendroidal sets as models for homotopy operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0902.1954"}> arXiv:0902.1954
              )
          %p
            making heavy use of results on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structures"} Cisinski model structures
            from
          %ul#Cisinski
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Les+pr%C3%A9faisceaux+comme+type+d%27homotopie"} Les préfaisceaux comme type d'homotopie
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/ast.pdf"} pdf
          %p A detailed discussion of the fibrant objects in the model structure is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ittay+Weiss"} Ittay Weiss
              %em On inner Kan complexes in the category of dendroidal sets
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science?_ob=ArticleURL&_udi=B6W9F-4VM2KC8-1&_user=457046&_rdoc=1&_fmt=&_orig=search&_sort=d&_docanchor=&view=c&_searchStrId=1115574112&_rerunOrigin=google&_acct=C000021878&_version=1&_urlVersion=0&_userid=457046&md5=5eb2307e02ed1aa9e6fe2c7809346546"}> web
              )
          %p
            The proof of the Quillen equivalence between the model structure on dendroidal sets and that on
            = succeed "-operads" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %ul#CisinskiMoerdijk11
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Dendroidal sets and simplicial operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.1004"}> arXiv:1109.1004
              )
          %p
            The relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+Cartesian+fibrations"} model structure for dendroidal Cartesian fibrations
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+left+fibrations"} model structure for dendroidal left fibrations
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gijs+Heuts"}> Gijs Heuts
              ,
              %em Algebras over infinity-Operads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.1776"}> arXiv:1110.1776
              )
        .revisedby
